There is an integer sequence A of length N whose values are unknown.
Given is an integer sequence B of length N-1 which is known to satisfy the following:
 B_i \geq \max(A_i, A_{i+1})
Find the maximum possible sum of the elements of A.
-----Constraints-----
 - All values in input are integers.
 - 2 \leq N \leq 100
 - 0 \leq B_i \leq 10^5
-----Input-----
Input is given from Standard Input in the following format:
N
B_1 B_2 ... B_{N-1}
-----Output-----
Print the maximum possible sum of the elements of A.
-----Sample Input-----
3
2 5
-----Sample Output-----
9
A can be, for example, ( 2 , 1 , 5 ), ( -1 , -2 , -3 ), or ( 2 , 2 , 5 ). Among those candidates, A = ( 2 , 2 , 5 ) has the maximum possible sum. \nUse Standard Input format
[code] import sys
def max_possible_sum(N, B):
    # Initialize the first two elements of A with the first two B values to make the problem easier to solve
    A = [B[0], max(B[0], B[1])]
    # Loop through the B values from index 2 to the end, updating the sum
    for i in range(2, N):
        A.append(min(A[i-1], B[i-1]) + A[i-2])
    return sum(A)
# Read input
N = int(sys.stdin.readline().strip())
B = list(map(int, sys.stdin.readline().strip().split()))
