Given a number N, change all bits at even positions to 0.
Example 1:
Input: N = 30
Output: 10
Explanation: Binary representation of
11110. Bits at Even positions are
highlighted. After making all of them
0, we get 01010. Hence the answer is 10.
Example 2:
Input:  N = 10
Output: 10
Explanation: Binary representation of
1010. Bits at Even positions are
highlighted. After making all of them
0, we get 1010. Hence the answer is 10.
Your Task:
You dont need to read input or print anything. Complete the function convertEvenBitToZero() which takes n as input parameter and returns the value of N after changing bits at even positions.
Expected Time Complexity: O(1)
Expected Auxiliary Space: O(1)
Constraints:
1<= N <=(32-bit number) #User function Template for python3
class Solutio...[+84 chars]
[code] class Solution:
    def convertEvenBitToZero(self, n):
        # XORing n with 1 will flip all bits at odd positions (which are at even positions in binary numbers)
        # Then we right-shift n by 1 to get the next bit position
        # This effectively changes all bits at even positions to 0
        return n ^ 1 << 1
