// true
is_alt("apple")
// false
is_alt("banana")
// true
```
Arguments consist of only lowercase letters. def is_alt(s):
	\nUse Call-Based format
[code] def is_alt(s):
    # Initialize counters for vowels and consonants
    vowel_count = 0
    consonant_count = 0
    special_char_count = 0
    # Iterate through each character in the string
    for char in s:
        if char in "aeiou":
            vowel_count += 1
        elif char.isalpha():
            consonant_count += 1
        else:
            special_char_count += 1
    # Check if the total number of characters is odd (as there are more vowels than consonants in an alternating pattern)
    return vowel_count == consonant_count + 1 or consonant_count == vowel_count + 1
# Test cases
